<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amol</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Amul</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amol is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mazandaran">Mazandaran</a> province, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, on the Haraz river near the Caspian coast. In the early Islamic centuries it was the chief city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabaristan">Tabaristan</a>, ruled in turn by local dynasties such as the Bavandids, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alids">Alids</a> and the Marashis. The historian al-Tabari was born there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/amol.jpg" alt="Amol" width="320" height="196" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ENMIRAN · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_of_the_Two_Historical_Bridges_of_Amol_at_Night.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
